  "body": "Research note / scoped decoder construction and lower bound. **No new kappa or hosted supplier.**\n\nIn the fixed bit label-decoder model on real E8, priced by rational pairing\nrank under PR446's inherited copy premise, nine orthogonal punctured root pairs\ngive an exact decoder of cost **54 on 102 ports**. A written argument supported\nby exact finite censuses bounds **cst/v >= 9/17** for every puncture of at most\n25 lines and any number of label terms. Equality occurs at 18 punctures; the\npackage gives explicit nine-term witnesses for every p=0..25.\n\nKeeping the selected PR589 reader basis fixed, one source dual is a root that\ncan be deleted to produce a P110 decoder with cost 62. A scope control changes\nthat basis and obtains two cost-6 terms but costs 68 overall. These are\nalgebraic decoders only. The fixed R439 inventory\npasses the aggregate capacity screen at v=110, whereas v=102 has only 408\nslots; no actual owner map, asymmetric copy, frame/restoration schedule or\ncomplete changed-supplier invoice is built.\n\nOnly `research/bit-orthogonal-pair-decoders/` is added. Exact base:\n`2921874911956718fcaaaf9396fe8267b3cfa9f0`. Selected pointers, `upstream/` and\nall existing packages remain unchanged. Source pins, literal witness,\ndeterministic receipt, proof, controls and validation are included.\n\nAt submission upstream had advanced to\n`abdc6a7002abdbcd9e21bfc5e1a795784deacfdf`; all seven pinned executable/data\ninputs remain byte-identical and PR942 remains selected. The research branch\nkeeps its exact recorded base rather than importing unrelated concurrent work.\n\nOne reproducible command, Python 3.10+ and standard library only:\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/bit-orthogonal-pair-decoders/test_package.py\n```\n\nThis runs the primary and a separate implementation, compares regenerated\nreceipt bytes, and tests corruption rejection. The primary refuses `-O`\nbecause the unchanged pinned pricing engines use assertions. Local execution\non CPython 3.12.14 and 3.13.15 and selected-source integrity checks are recorded\nin `VALIDATION.md`; no whole-repository suite or hosted CI pass is claimed.\n\nPR620 identified the orthogonal-pair mechanism; PR757 and PR761 certify the\nfixed P111 floor; PR595 named the unrealised 54/102 unit. This contribution adds\na literal exact decoder and a puncture-independent rational pairing-cost\nbound, not priority for those predecessor observations. PR968 is the distinct\ncomplex frame-pair analogue, with a different cost. Recent PR1020 uses complex\nF2 label ranks at 26 punctures and PR1008 uses fixed-P111 tensor shears; neither\nduplicates this scope. The immediate refresh through #1081 also found PR1077's\ncomplex-coefficient extension of PR968, another distinct eight-term model.\nCredit and exact source heads are retained in\n`NOTICE.md` and `SOURCES.json`.\n\nInherited parabolic coverage, copy interpretation, compiler, hosting,\nprecision/tape and analytic obligations remain explicit. The written argument\nand finite replay are not proof-assistant verification of multiplication or\nindependent human review. Prepared for @navinor with substantial\nAI assistance through OpenCode; resumed review/packaging used GPT-6.1 Sol\n(OpenAI). Apache-2.0. Structural-decoder track, OS assignment seed 40; no pinned\ncoordination issue existed, so the claim is local.\n",
